 "final_message": "Application BHL-26001 is submitted, and I recorded your intent to proceed. Brightpath's page confirmed the intent (\"Intent to proceed received\"). The application status still reads \"Loan Estimate issued; conditional review.\"\n\n- **Application:** I submitted it once, with credit-check and e-sign consent. I also gave the required certification that the information is true and complete, which the form needs for submission. I uploaded the last 2 statements for each of your four personal accounts (Aug and Sep 2026) and the last 2 payslips each (Oct 2 and Oct 16). Nadia's Northgate business checking account stayed out of it, and nothing went to anyone but Brightpath.\n- **Underwriting condition:** The underwriter asked about an $8,000 deposit on 09/03/2026 into Sam's checking account ending 4417. You told me it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, not a loan. I sent that as the written explanation.\n- **Loan Estimate:** It was within all your limits, so I signed the intent to proceed with both your names.\n\n| | Estimate | Your limit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Interest rate | 6.25% | 6.5% |\n| Monthly payment | $3,042.41 | $3,100 |\n| Closing costs | $12,850 | $14,000 |\n\nThe estimate is for a $440,000, 30-year fixed loan. Estimated cash to close is $122,850, and the rate lock is available for 45 days.",
